## [ENT-004] | 2026-11-15 19:46 UTC | Unity | order | ref: game/routes/plan.json | see: ENT-003
Changed: on Suggi's word of 2026-11-15 the repository's folders players, planets, factions, map, routes, rules and fleet moved into the new group game/ (game/routes/plan.json, game/fleet/, game/rules/); every path in this entry carries its new name, and the wording of the orders is otherwise that of ENT-003. An Admiral that keeps an old path in its own notes or scripts changes it at its next session.
In force from 2026-11-15 19:46 UTC until a newer entry.
FLEET
F1. The Fleet Admiral commands every ship: the service dispatch flies each pilot along its role's list in game/routes/plan.json. No Admiral commands a ship or changes the plan until an entry here hands its division over.
  Goal: one hand on the fleet while it is built.
  Changes when: Suggi hands a division to its Admiral.
F2. Posture HOLD toward every player and every NPC ship, for every division: never initiate; flee, dock or brace (rulebook 8.2). Wildlife of the role grazer may be hunted in Voidborn space by the ships the plan sends.
  Goal: no loss while every ship is a starter.
  Changes when: an entry here sets TIGHT or FREE for a division and a region.
F3. Every ship stays in policed Voidborn space.
  Goal: no loss while every ship is a starter.
  Changes when: an entry here sends one ship out, insured and with an empty hold (rulebook 8.3).
F4. No pilot of ours writes to another player. A contact is passed to the Fleet Admiral.
  Goal: diplomacy has one voice.
  Changes when: approved templates exist.
F5. No new pilot without Suggi's word. The size he ordered on 2026-11-15: 40 miner-, 20 trader-, 20 hauler-, 30 drone- and 20 scout- ships, and the command group of F10. A new pilot runs its three starter missions and then flies its role's list like every other.
  Goal: permanent choices are Suggi's.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F7. Every pilot keeps 3,000 cr in its wallet.
  Goal: the weekly tax is taken from the wallet (Voidborn: 6% of the week's income, 0.75% of the ship's value); next assessment about 2026-11-16 12:00 UTC.
  Changes when: the tax is prepaid, or the rates change.
F8. No ship is idle. Every ship works, all the time, the first open route of its role's list: one that pays, or else one that trains its pilot. A turn lasts four hours; at its end the plan is set again from what the runs measured (game/routes/index.md).
  Goal: every ship earns or levels, and a ship born later climbs the same ladder without a hand.
  Changes when: Suggi's word; a route that loses money and trains nothing its ships need leaves the plan.
F9. A hunter fights grazers of 100 hull or less, one hunter per place, and flees under 60% hull or when a ship joins the fight.
  Goal: no ship lost to a hunt.
  Changes when: a hull is tested against bigger prey and its route says so.
F10. The command group is the Fleet Admiral's own division, Command: six flagships (the Fleet Admiral's command ship and one captain ship per Admiral) and their guard, the sentinel- ships. The group flies one list of routes (the roles command and sentinel in game/routes/plan.json) and the dispatcher flies it like every ship. An Admiral lists its flagship in its FLEET.md and commands it no more than its other ships (F1).
  Goal: the fleet's command moves as one group under one hand (Suggi, 2026-11-15).
  Changes when: Suggi's word; the group flies in formation once a route of its own exists.
F11. The faction The Collective (tag CLTV) exists since 2026-11-15. Its leader is the Fleet Admiral's flagship; its members are the command group; its cap reads 50 members and a recruitment office raises it. Inviting, joining, leaving, a role, a war, peace, an alliance and every word in the faction's name are the Fleet Admiral's, on Suggi's word. No other pilot of ours joins any faction.
  Goal: one voice toward other players, and a faction that stays ours.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
TURN
T4. 2026-11-15 19:00 to 23:00 UTC. The plan of game/routes/plan.json: every pilot flies the two one-time circuits once (the substrate delivery, the two-mission circuit); drones hunt veil-rays at the two grazing grounds, ranched (no hunt below four animals, four kills a run), and sell at Node Beta; one drone tries the drift-rays of the home cloud; one ship waits at the Bellatrix belt for thorium; scouts read each Voidborn system every half hour; every other ship mines for skill, ore into storage. The 75 new pilots join their role's list as their starter missions end.
  Done when: each route of the plan has its measured figure in game/routes/index.md and the plan of the next turn is set from them.
EVERY ADMIRAL
Order: each turn, read this entry, the state of your ships (the fleet folder of the unit's data), the figures of the routes they fly (game/routes/index.md) and their last run logs. Report what your ships did, earned and cost, what failed, and one proposal that would raise your measure, with its numbers. Keep your FLEET.md current: your division's ships as the fleet folder lists them, and your flagship.
Limits: F1 holds. You fly no ship, start no runner and change no file of game/routes/ or game/fleet/. Reading is free: the data folder, and calls through the gate that only read, for your own ships. A proposal goes into Suggestions of your session entry and into your report. What your division needs from another division or from me is a request in requests.log, one entry each; at every session start you answer the open requests addressed to you. While F1 holds, a request that needs a ship moved is mine to answer: I change the plan. The shared skill fleet-play says how each kind of work is done.
ZERO, Mining (the miner- ships)
Order: find mined goods that pay. From what the fields of our space hold (the scouting files) and what our stations bid for or make things from (the market files, the catalog's recipes), name the one chain most worth a test with one ship: what to mine, where, what to make of it, where to sell it, and the credits per ship-hour you expect.
Found 2026-11-15: stations bid 300 cr for uranium ore and 240 cr for thorium ore, thousands of units each, and their two deposits in our space read 0; a mining run costs 150 to 170 cr per ship-hour, all of it fuel for the trips to a station in another system; the same run at a belt beside a station cost 0 but the belt was empty. Say also how training can cost less.
Measure: credits per ship-hour of the mining routes (today below zero: common ore sells for 1 to 4 cr); the Mining level of your pilots.
MERCURY, Trade (the trader- ships)
Order: find a trade that holds. From the order books the census saves every half hour, name the price gaps between two of our stations that held in two reads in a row and cover fuel and the 1% sales tax, and the station-need missions on the boards that goods of ours could fill. Propose one circuit route with a price cap and a price floor.
Found 2026-11-15, not tested: control nodes have bids of 784 cr for 400 units at Node Gamma and Node Beta and are made by hand from 2 circuit boards, 4 copper wiring, 1 gold wiring and 1 silver wiring, all on offer at our stations, the two wirings by the unit. Work out what one craft costs at today's offers, how many crafts the offers allow, and whether the chain is worth one ship.
Measure: credits per ship-hour from buying and selling (today: no such route).
APOLLO, Logistics (the hauler- ships)
Order: know what the fleet owns and where. List the goods in our holds and in storage by station, and say for each where it sells or what it feeds. Work out the fuel a starter burns per jump and on each route of the plan. Propose one hauling circuit that turns stored goods into credits, or a cheaper home station for a route.
Found 2026-11-15: the mining runs since 17:10 UTC took about 10,000 units of iron and copper ore to Node Beta and Synchrony Hub by their records (the storage itself was not read today); the game's guides name two recipes any station workshop runs (steel plate from iron ore, copper wiring from copper ore). Read the storage, and say what that ore is worth made into something.
Measure: credits recovered from stored goods; fuel per ship-hour of the fleet's routes.
APOPHIS, Military (the drone- ships)
Order: make hunting pay more and lose nothing. From the hunt runs and the herd counts (the wildlife files), give for each hunting place the kills and credits per hunter-hour, the damage taken and how the herd changed. Say which place to add or to rest, and whether a railgun per hunter pays for itself. Name the armed pilots seen at our hunting grounds (game/players/index.md).
Found 2026-11-15: the two veil-ray herds pay 3,300 and 3,600 cr per hunter-hour over four runs each and hold 6 and 7 animals; verdigris curd has bids of 330 cr for about 240 units at five stations, whale oil 300 cr for about 240 units, radiant bile 780 cr for about 210 units; six urchin kills gave no bile; a whale (220 hull) took a starter to 15 hull. Say what hull and fit a whale hunter needs and what it costs.
Measure: credits per hunter-hour; ships lost, which stays 0.
ORACLE, Intel (the scout- ships)
Order: keep the fleet's picture fresh and find what we cannot see yet. Check that every Voidborn system was read within the last hour (the scouting, market, missions and wildlife files) and that the intel files and their indexes are current. Name the three places beyond Voidborn space most worth one scout: the route, its risk and what we would look for there. Sending it is Suggi's decision (F3).
New 2026-11-15: game/factions/ holds the player factions with a base or with pilots in our space, and game/factions/index.md the zones they hold; the hourly tracker writes it. Read it with the other indexes, and name the factions whose pilots are most often in our space.
Measure: the age of the oldest system read; intel files added or corrected.

## [ENT-005] | 2026-11-15 21:09 UTC | Unity | order | ref: game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md | see: ENT-004
Changed: on Suggi's word of 2026-11-15 every division is handed to its Admiral: each Admiral commands its own ships, keeps its own plan and its own guidebook, and tests what could pay (F1, F14). No ship works at a loss to fill time: mining for skill ends, a ship without paying work waits docked (F8). Missions that pay once are flown first, without asking (F8). Money for tests has a limit (F12). The fleet goes beyond Voidborn space: the scouts, the Military division and the command group (F2, F3, F13; rulebook 8.3 changed on Suggi's word). The plan is one file per role (game/routes/plans/<role>.json; game/routes/plan.json is gone). A turn is the four hours between two scheduled runs. The blocks of the Admirals are new.
In force from 2026-11-15 21:20 UTC until a newer entry.
GOAL (Suggi, 2026-11-15)
First income that repeats in every division. Then a faction with shared storage and a first supply chain. Then stations and bases of our own beyond the safe zone: strong and independent, not hiding. Every order below serves the first step.
FLEET
F1. Each Admiral commands the ships of its own division, by the word before the dash of a pilot's name: miner- Zero, trader- Mercury, hauler- Apollo, drone- Apophis, scout- Oracle. The Fleet Admiral commands the command group (F10) and may command any ship. Every command goes through the scripts of game/fleet/ (game/fleet/index.md): they refuse a ship of another division and a ship another program is flying. No call goes to the gate around them.
  Goal: every division finds its own income, and no two hands drive one ship.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F2. Posture HOLD toward every player and every NPC ship, in policed space and for every ship: never initiate; flee, dock or brace (rulebook 8.2). Outside policed space the Military division and the command group are TIGHT: they may fight pirates and wildlife, and a pilot only when it attacks us first; every other ship stays HOLD there too. Wildlife is hunted inside F9.
  Goal: no loss we did not choose. Outside it is dangerous; Suggi accepts that for the ships of F13.
  Changes when: an entry here sets FREE for a region, which needs Suggi's word.
F3. Every ship stays in policed Voidborn space, except the ships F13 sends out.
  Goal: a ship is risked where the risk can pay.
  Changes when: an entry here.
F4. No pilot of ours writes to another player. A contact is passed to the Fleet Admiral.
  Goal: diplomacy has one voice.
  Changes when: approved templates exist.
F5. No new pilot without Suggi's word. The size he ordered on 2026-11-15: 40 miner-, 20 trader-, 20 hauler-, 30 drone- and 20 scout- ships, and the command group of F10. No pilot is registered only for its starter rewards (rulebook 8.1). A division grows when it shows paying work for more ships than it has.
  Goal: permanent choices are Suggi's.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F7. Every pilot keeps 3,000 cr in its wallet.
  Goal: the weekly tax is taken from the wallet (Voidborn: 6% of the week's income, 0.75% of the ship's value); next assessment about 2026-11-16 12:30 UTC.
  Changes when: the tax is prepaid, or the rates change.
F8. No ship works at a loss to fill time. A free ship flies the first open route of its role's plan (game/routes/plans/<role>.json). A plan holds, in this order: the missions that pay once, the routes that pay, tests with one ship, and last the route park: dock at home and wait, which costs nothing. A mission that pays once is flown by every pilot as soon as its route exists: nobody asks first. A route that loses money leaves the plan at once.
  Goal: the fleet's credits rise. Measured 2026-11-15: mining iron and copper for skill cost about 160 cr per ship-hour, 22,000 cr an hour for the fleet, and the ore has no buyer.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F9. A hunter fights grazers of 100 hull or less, one hunter per place, and flees under 60% hull or when a ship joins the fight. The Military division may test bigger prey and other fits: one ship per test, the flee rule kept, hull and fit written into the route.
  Goal: no ship lost to a hunt.
  Changes when: a hull is tested against bigger prey and its route says so.
F10. The command group is the Fleet Admiral's own division, Command: six flagships (the Fleet Admiral's command ship and one captain ship per Admiral) and their guard, the sentinel- ships. The group flies one plan (the roles command and sentinel). An Admiral lists its flagship in its FLEET.md; the flagship flies with the command group, under the Fleet Admiral's hand.
  Goal: the fleet's command moves as one group under one hand (Suggi, 2026-11-15).
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F11. The faction The Collective (tag CLTV) exists since 2026-11-15. Its leader is the Fleet Admiral's flagship; its members are the command group; its cap reads 50 members. Inviting, joining, leaving, a role, a war, peace, an alliance and every word in the faction's name are the Fleet Admiral's, on Suggi's word. No other pilot of ours joins any faction.
  Goal: one voice toward other players, and a faction that stays ours.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F12. Money. An Admiral spends only the wallets of its own ships and never takes one below F7. On tests (a module, goods for a trade or a craft, a hull) a division spends at most 10% of its ships' credits in one turn; Military 25%, for weapons and hulls. Before goods are bought for a mission, a trade or a craft: one ship, one unit of the test, the answer read. Nothing is given away, jettisoned or sold under a standing bid to empty a hold or a storage.
  Goal: a test that fails costs little. On 2026-11-15 about 92,000 cr went into goods for a mission that hands them out.
  Changes when: a division shows income that repeats.
F13. Beyond Voidborn space (Suggi, 2026-11-15: "we go hard", it is dangerous, and we need to make money). The fleet scouts the lawless systems next to ours for income and for a place where a base could stand: Achernar, Ruchbah, Cedarhold and Garnet by way of The Experiment, Ironhollow by Pherkad, Schedar by Node Beta; then Atlas and Intercrus. Who goes: the scouts, who read each system whole (game/routes/census-frontier.json, kept by Oracle); the Military division, which looks at what lives there and what a drone can fight; the command group, which flies the same census under the Fleet Admiral's hand. Every ship goes with an empty hold and comes home to a Voidborn station to sell or store. A ship lost is an entry in errors.log with its cause, and the system where it was lost leaves the census list until Military has looked at it. Mining, Trade and Logistics follow: each may send one ship, hold empty, to a system the census has read, when its file shows a field or a bid worth the trip.
  Goal: find what pays more than our six systems do, and see what the miners, traders and haulers can do there.
  Changes when: the reports of the first reads.
F14. Knowledge. Each Admiral keeps its guidebook, game/routes/guidebook/<division>.md: the routes that pay with their measured figures, what did not pay and why, how its pilots level, the hull and the fit for its work. Every member reads the others'. A figure comes from routes.py measure or a run's RESULT line, never from memory. What an Admiral means to do next stands in `planned` of its plan file.
  Goal: every ship born later starts where the others stand, and five Admirals do not test the same thing twice.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
TURN
T5. From this entry until the next. A turn is the four hours between two scheduled runs: the Admirals at 00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00 and 20:00 UTC (Zero on the hour, then Apollo, Mercury, Apophis and Oracle five minutes apart), the Fleet Admiral one hour after them. The scheduled runs are off until Suggi's go; a run is started by hand until then. At the handover every plan holds the missions that pay once and park; the drones' plan the two veil-ray hunts; the scouts' plan the census of our space and the census of the frontier; the command group's plan the census of the frontier.
  Done when: each Admiral's report names one test it flew with its credits per ship-hour after all costs, its plan and its guidebook are committed, and none of its ships is left held by hand.
EVERY ADMIRAL
Order: you command your division's ships. Each turn: (1) read the board and the books: `python3 -I -B game/fleet/division.py me`, `game/fleet/board.py all`, `game/fleet/ledger.py show`, game/routes/index.md, your guidebook and the others'. (2) Keep your plan: missions that pay once first, then what pays, best first, then park. (3) Fly at least one test that could raise your measure: one ship, by hand or as a route with max_ships 1; read its RESULT line; work out the credits per ship-hour after every cost. (4) Write what the test showed into your guidebook and what you mean to do next into `planned`. (5) Report what your ships did, earned and cost, with fuel and repair named where a record holds them, what failed, and what you need from me: a route, a runner's step, a skill, data. The shared skill fleet-play says how; your FLEET.md lists your ships.
Limits: F1 to F14. Your own ships only, and beyond Voidborn space only as F13 says; what you need from another division is a request in requests.log, and you answer the open requests addressed to you at every session start. You write your plan, the routes your ships fly and your guidebook; a script of game/fleet/, a route another division flies too and another role's plan change by a request. Release every ship you took by hand before your turn ends. What these orders do not cover is a request to me, never a guess.
ZERO, Mining (the miner- ships)
Order: make one mined good pay. First, on Suggi's word, energy crystal: mine it with one ship at the nebula of game/routes/hunt-gsc-veil-ray.json (agree the place with Apophis, whose hunter works there), make focused crystal of it, sell it where a bid stands, and report the credits per ship-hour after every cost: fuel, parts bought, the tax on the sale. The craft is flown by hand first (gate.py raw, storage and craft); write down each call and its answer: the runner's craft step is built from that record. Then the next goods by the same test: the ice harvester and honeyglobe, titanium ore (the mission Titanium Extraction Contract pays 3,500 cr on five boards; where titanium lies is not known), uranium and thorium ore (bids of 300 and 240 cr; both deposits in our space read 0). No ship mines iron or copper for storage.
Found 2026-11-15: focused crystal had a bid of 1,466 cr for 879 units at The Experiment (18:59 UTC); the carbon belt at Acubens held 1,002 carbon ore, enough for First Steps in the Void for about 60 pilots.
Measure: credits per ship-hour of your best route after all costs; the number of your ships on a route that pays.
MERCURY, Trade (the trader- ships)
Order: find a trade that pays and holds. The moves of every best bid and ask are kept now (`game/fleet/ledger.py prices <item>`): name the gaps that held over several reads and cover fuel and the 1% tax, and test the best with one ship and a few units. Fly the control-node craft by hand with one trader and write down each call and its answer. Fly game/routes/voidborn-concurrent.json once by hand: it buys nothing and shows whether Concurrent Approval hands its goods out. 52 pilots still hold Market Participation: Selling (1,000 cr each for ten units of anything sold on the exchange): say where ten units of what we hold still find a bid, in queue.log, for the Admirals whose pilots hold it. Name the markets beyond Voidborn space the scout should read first, and what we would sell or buy there.
Found 2026-11-15: no gap between two of our stations held with depth; Node Beta's saved book showed a bid of 692 cr for neural soma that cost about 313 cr at the capital, quantity not recorded.
Measure: credits per ship-hour from buying and selling; one-time credits collected.
APOLLO, Logistics (the hauler- ships)
Order: turn what lies in storage into credits, and carry for the others. The storage book is kept by itself now (`game/fleet/ledger.py show all`): from it and the recipes, say what each stored good is worth made into something, and fly one craft by hand with one hauler (steel plate, copper wiring or ferrous slugs from the stored ore), each call and its answer written down. Work out the fuel a starter burns per jump, so that every Admiral can cost a route. Say which station should be the fleet's storage home. Carry what another division asks for in requests.log.
Found 2026-11-15: about 9,000 units of iron and copper ore lie in the haulers' storage at three stations and no station bids for them; the spare neural soma of the Substrate mission lie with them.
Measure: credits recovered from stored goods; requests of other divisions carried out.
APOPHIS, Military (the drone- ships)
Order: hunting pays; make it pay more, then design the ships for battle. Test freely inside F9 and F12: the railgun and other weapons on a hunter, bigger prey with one ship, other herds in our space; for each test write hull, fit, kills, damage taken and credits per hunter-hour into your guidebook. Then name the hull and the fit the Military division flies next (hull tier 2 needs Piloting 10), what it costs and what it would earn. Keep one hunter on each veil-ray herd, ranched: no hunt below four animals, four kills a run. Answer Zero on the nebula. Beyond our space (F13, TIGHT): send drones after the scouts' first reads, one ship per test: which herds are there, what a pirate does to a starter and a starter to a pirate, what pays; write the place, the fit and the result of every fight into your guidebook.
Found 2026-11-15: the two veil-ray herds pay about 3,100 and 3,350 cr per hunter-hour; drift-rays at home lost 270 cr per hunter-hour over ten runs; six urchin kills gave no bile; a whale (220 hull) took a starter to 15 hull.
Measure: credits per hunter-hour; ships lost, which stays 0.
ORACLE, Intel (the scout- ships)
Order: lead the reading of the frontier (F13) and keep the picture fresh. game/routes/census-frontier.json is yours: the systems on its list, how often, how many ships at once; it starts with the six systems next to our border and four ships at a time, and Atlas and Intercrus join when the fuel for the way is known. For each system: the fields and what is left in them, stations with their order books and boards, herds, pirates, pilots and factions met, and whether a base could stand there. Say in queue.log what each read found that another division can use. Keep every Voidborn system read within the hour; `every_minutes` of game/routes/census-voidborn.json is yours to set. The game moved from 0.715.2 to 0.717.0 on 2026-11-15: read what changed and name every line of game/rules/ it makes wrong, in a request to me.
Found 2026-11-15: 3,374 pilots were online and 16,009 registered (the game's public figures, 20:55 UTC); the largest factions count 1,249, 306 and 274 members.
Measure: systems beyond Voidborn space read; the age of the oldest Voidborn read.

