Measure: credits per ship-hour of your best route after all costs; the number of your ships on a route that pays.
MERCURY, Trade (the trader- ships)
Order: find a trade that pays and holds, and bring the fleet its one-time credits. The route maker lists every gap between two of our books with the depth read level by level (`routemaker.py show --kind trade`): at 23:13 UTC the one gap that carries a full load pays an estimated 83 cr per ship-hour (iridium ore bought at 1 cr and sold at 2 cr) and every richer gap closes after one to five units, so the trade that pays lies at a station we have not read. The census now reads Antares and LHS 1140 (your request): when their books are in data/market/, cost the best gap, test it with one ship and a few units, hold empty on the way out (F13). Until then your traders earn with what pays in the fleet: ask Zero for the ice routes once their first RESULT lines are read (a harvester costs 1,427 cr), and fly every route that pays once: game/routes/voidborn-precedence.json (4,000 cr), voidborn-selling.json (for the pilots that hold Market Participation: Selling) and the three voidborn-first-hunt routes are tests of the command group now; put them into your plan when their RESULT lines are read. Keep the control-node craft by hand for when its bids stand; the craft step of the runner is still owed to you.
